---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = "Google Privacy Policy Analysis 2026";
const description = "Comprehensive analysis of Google's privacy policy covering data collection, advertising practices, third-party sharing, and privacy controls. Updated for 2026.";
const keywords = "Google privacy policy analysis, Google data collection, Google advertising privacy, Google privacy controls, Google account data";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} keywords={keywords}>
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="separator">›</span>
      <a href="/brand-analysis">Brand Analysis</a>
      <span class="separator">›</span>
      <span class="current">Google</span>
    </nav>

    <article class="brand-analysis">
      <header class="brand-header">
        <div class="brand-badge google">High Data Collection</div>
        <h1>Google Privacy Policy Analysis 2026</h1>
        <p class="brand-tagline">Comprehensive breakdown of Google's data practices, advertising model, and privacy controls</p>
      </header>

      <section class="analysis-section">
        <h2>What Data Google Collects</h2>
        <p>Google collects an extensive amount of data across its ecosystem of products and services. This includes search history, location data, YouTube viewing history, Gmail content, Chrome browsing activity, and device information. The company aggregates data from over 30+ products including Search, YouTube, Gmail, Chrome, Android, Maps, and Nest.</p>
        
        <div class="key-finding warning">
          <h4>Key Finding: Comprehensive Data Aggregation</h4>
          <p>Google combines data across services to create detailed user profiles used for advertising targeting and personalization.</p>
        </div>

        <ul class="data-list">
          <li><strong>Search Data:</strong> Every search query, voice search, and image search</li>
          <li><strong>Location History:</strong> Precise GPS coordinates, visited places, and travel patterns</li>
          <li><strong>YouTube Activity:</strong> Videos watched, search history, comments, and interactions</li>
          <li><strong>Communication Data:</strong> Email content, attached files, and calendar entries in Gmail</li>
          <li><strong>Device Data:</strong> App usage, crashes, and system activity on Android devices</li>
          <li><strong>Voice Data:</strong> Voice commands and audio recordings from Google Assistant</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="analysis-section">
        <h2>Advertising Data Practices</h2>
        <p>Google's advertising business generated over $237 billion in revenue in 2025, making it the largest digital advertising platform globally. The company builds detailed advertising profiles using:</p>

        <ul class="data-list">
          <li>Cross-site browsing behavior through Google Analytics</li>
          <li>Purchase intent signals from search history</li>
          <li>Demographic information from account data</li>
          <li>Interest categories derived from YouTube and search behavior</li>
          <li>Remarketing lists from visited websites</li>
          <li>Offline purchase data from participating retailers</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="key-finding warning">
          <h4>Advertising Profile Accuracy</h4>
          <p>Google's algorithms infer sensitive attributes including political views, health conditions, and personal relationships from behavioral data.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="analysis-section">
        <h2>Third-Party Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>Google shares data with various third parties under specific circumstances. This includes advertising partners, analytics providers, device manufacturers, government agencies, and service providers. The company's partnership network spans thousands of companies.</p>

        <div class="key-finding danger">
          <h4>Data Broker Relationships</h4>
          <p>Google participates in real-time bidding advertising exchanges, where bid requests containing user identifiers are shared with thousands of advertisers simultaneously.</p>
        </div>

        <h3>When Google Shares Your Data</h3>
        <ul class="data-list">
          <li>With your consent for specific services</li>
          <li>With advertisers for ad targeting (with some controls)</li>
          <li>With legal authorities responding to valid requests</li>
          <li>With service providers maintaining Google services</li>
          <li>With analytics and measurement partners</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="analysis-section">
        <h2>Privacy Controls Available</h2>
        <p>Google provides several privacy controls through your Google Account, though many are buried in settings menus. Key controls include:</p>

        <ul class="data-list">
          <li><strong>Activity Controls:</strong> Pause or delete search history, location history, YouTube history</li>
          <li><strong>Ad Personalization:</strong> Disable or limit ad personalization settings</li>
          <li><strong>Data Export:</strong> Download all your Google data through Takeout</li>
          <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> Delete your entire account and associated data</li>
          <li><strong>Incognito Mode:</strong> Browse without saving to account history</li>
          <li><strong>Privacy Checkup:</strong> Guided review of privacy settings</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="key-finding info">
          <h4>Control Limitations</h4>
          <p>Some privacy controls are device-specific or service-specific, meaning you must configure them separately for each product and device.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="analysis-section">
        <h2>AI-Powered Analysis Summary</h2>
        <div class="summary-box">
          <h3>Privacy Risk Assessment: <span class="risk-high">HIGH</span></h3>
          <p>Google's business model is fundamentally built on data collection and advertising. The company has the most comprehensive view of user behavior of any company globally, combining search, location, communication, and browsing data.</p>
          
          <h4>Primary Concerns:</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Extensive cross-service data aggregation</li>
            <li>Detailed advertising profiles with inferred sensitive attributes</li>
            <li>Real-time bidding participation exposes data to thousands of entities</li>
            <li>Complex, scattered privacy controls difficult to fully utilize</li>
            <li>Historical data retention even after account deletion</li>
          </ul>

          <h4>Positive Aspects:</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Provides detailed privacy controls (when configured)</li>
            <li>Offers data export and deletion capabilities</li>
            <li>Regular transparency reports on government requests</li>
            <li>Annual privacy policy updates with clearer explanations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="cta-section">
        <h3>Analyze Google's Actual Privacy Policy</h3>
        <p>Paste Google's current privacy policy to get our AI-powered analysis with specific clause breakdowns, risk scoring, and plain English explanations.</p>
        <a href="/" class="btn-primary">Analyze Policy Now</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .breadcrumbs {
    padding: 24px 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .breadcrumbs a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .breadcrumbs a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .separator {
    margin: 0 8px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .current {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .brand-analysis {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 0;
  }

  .brand-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .brand-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .brand-badge.google {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(66, 133, 244, 0.2), rgba(234, 67, 53, 0.2));
    border: 1px solid rgba(66, 133, 244, 0.4);
    color: #4285f4;
  }

  .brand-header h1 {
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--text-primary), var(--text-secondary));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .brand-tagline {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .analysis-section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding: 32px;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .analysis-section h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .analysis-section h3 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 24px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .analysis-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .key-finding {
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin: 24px 0;
    border-left: 4px solid;
  }

  .key-finding h4 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .key-finding p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .key-finding.warning {
    background: rgba(255, 193, 7, 0.1);
    border-color: #ffc107;
  }

  .key-finding.warning h4 {
    color: #ffc107;
  }

  .key-finding.danger {
    background: rgba(255, 82, 82, 0.1);
    border-color: #ff5252;
  }

  .key-finding.danger h4 {
    color: #ff5252;
  }

  .key-finding.info {
    background: rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.1);
    border-color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .key-finding.info h4 {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .data-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .data-list li {
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .data-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .data-list li strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .summary-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-secondary), var(--bg-card));
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .summary-box h3 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .risk-high {
    color: #ff5252;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .summary-box h4 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    margin: 20px 0 12px;
  }

  .summary-box ul {
    list-style: disc;
    margin-left: 20px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .summary-box ul li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 48px 32px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.1), rgba(255, 0, 128, 0.1));
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .cta-section h3 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    max-width: 500px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 16px 32px;
    background: var(--gradient-primary);
    color: white;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-glow);
    color: white;
  }
</style>